# November 24, 2026: Carnegie libraries of New Jersey, a batch of the pass the owner asked for to put the buildings
# Andrew Carnegie paid for on the map. Started from Wikipedia's "List of Carnegie libraries in New Jersey" (36 libraries
# from grants of 1900 to 1917) and Dubicki's article "Carnegie Libraries in New Jersey: 1900-1923" (New Jersey Studies,
# 2017). This batch: thirty of them, standing, ruined or gone; six more are leads in the note. Sources opened in this
# session: Wikipedia as raw text, the libraries' own pages (hours, histories), National Register nominations, state
# preservation pages, HMdb, local papers and borough pages, read through the web fetch tool.
# Pins: ArcGIS geocoder points for the street addresses, OpenStreetMap or Wikipedia points, looked at on the leaf-off aerial.
